title Straight from a throw-in
intro Blue is taking a throw-in near Red's goal.
flip vertical

setup
  lineup 7v7
  player B-RB at 70, 67
  player R-CB at 76, 40
  player R-LB at 74, 22
  player B-LF at 88, 52
  ball with B-RB

step
  caption Watch where Blue is when the ball is played. The yellow line marks the last defender.
  label B-RB Throw
  draw sideline bottom
  draw line 76, 0 to 76, 68

step
  caption Blue throws it to a teammate who is past the last Red defender.
  ball to 86, 52
  arrow from B-RB to ball
  draw line 76, 0 to 76, 68
  duration 1300

question
  prompt Is the Blue striker offside?
  answer No
  wrong Yes
  wrong Yes, they are past the defender
  wrong Only if they score
  correct Not offside.
  why There is no offside from a throw-in. You can stand anywhere and take the ball.

question
  prompt What if a teammate had kicked it instead?
  answer Then it would be offside
  wrong Still fine
  wrong It would be a corner
  wrong Red would get a penalty
  correct Then it would be offside.
  why A kicked pass counts for offside. A throw-in does not, so a throw is a good way to reach a teammate far up the field.
